Thu Nov 19 13:19:21 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 2.5.13
  * Security fixes:
    + ReDoS in coordinate name finder regex patterns
      (CVE-2026-120404)
    + Untrusted Java deserialization in SvmDoccatModel
      (bsc#1270446, CVE-2026-43825, OPENNLP-1823)
    + ReDoS / stack exhaustion in RegexNameFinderFactory built-in
      EMAIL and URL patterns (bsc#1280293, CVE-2026-82617,
      OPENNLP-1922)
    + Arbitrary Class Instantiation via XML Feature Generator
      Descriptor and Format Name (bsc#1272520, CVE-2026-63317,
      OPENNLP-1890, OPENNLP-1891)
  * Changes of version 2.5.13
    + Thread safety: TokenizerME no longer changes the shared
      WhitespaceTokenizer.INSTANCE, and MorfologikTagDictionary,
      AbstractModel and AbstractClassPathModelFinder.findModels can
      be shared between threads.
    + Deep learning: SentenceVectorsDL runs on a GPU,
      DocumentCategorizerDL computes a numerically stable softmax,
      invalid document split options are rejected instead of looping
      forever, and close() can be called more than once.
    + Model downloads: DownloadUtil uses a local copy of the model
      index when the model host cannot be reached and verifies cached
      models against their SHA-512 checksum.
    + Format readers and data: the AD readers no longer hang at end
      of file or fail on the FlorestaVirgem corpus, the bundled
      Spanish head rules match tags with escaped dots, and
      MarkableFileInputStream and the Leipzig reader release their
      file handles.
    + BaseModel loads on Android, and StringUtil.toUpperCase maps
      supplementary-plane letters.
    + Release artifacts: the binary distribution LICENSE covers all
      bundled third-party code.
  * Summary of changes since 1.9.5:
    + Changes of 2.5.x:
      - Thread-safe implementations of key components (sentence
        detector, tokenizer, POS-tagger, probabilistic ME classes)
      - Classpath loading of pre-trained models (opennlp-models)
      - Support for Roberta-based models
      - Support for custom abbreviation dictionaries
      - Verification of cached models against SHA-512 checksums
      - Dropped Brat Annotator component to sandbox (removes Jackson
        and Jersey dependencies)
    + Changes of 2.4.0:
      - New module to load pre-trained OpenNLP models from JARs on
        the classpath
    + Changes of 2.3.x:
      - Raise minimum Java version to 17
      - Split opennlp-dl into CPU and GPU variants
      - Address memory issue with String interning in large
        dictionaries (OPENNLP-421)
      - Abbreviation dictionaries for multiple languages
    + Changes of 2.2.0:
      - Introduce SLF4J logging to replace System.out
      - ONNX Runtime support for sentence-transformers
    + Changes of 2.1.x:
      - Optional GPU inference in ONNX Runtime configuration
      - Unlimited text length in document classification with ONNX
    + Changes of 2.0.0:
      - Raise minimum Java requirement to Java 11
      - Support model inference using ONNX Runtime (opennlp-dl)
      - Download pre-trained models from within Apache OpenNLP
      - Support for MASC corpus format
- Removed patch:
  * opennlp-CVE-2026-63317.patch
    + not needed with this version

